(117, NULL, 70, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-24', 'followup', 87, 3, 'completed', 17, 'BAGAMBIKI Hubertt', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 60.00, 100.00, 60.00, NULL, '2026-09-04 06:14:13', NULL, NULL, '2026-08-24 11:59:40', '2026-09-04 06:14:13', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(118, NULL, 107, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-06', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 8, 'NIYINGENERA Thierry', 1, NULL, 'To do maintenance of fire alarm system and water based fire fighting system.\r\nTo do maintenance of failed CCTV cameras and increase storage capacity to 3 months.\r\nTo install the lightning system that can cover the whole compound of station.\r\nTo provide calibration certificate, retail license and occupation permit via email.\r\nEmail noted at the bottom', NULL, NULL, 86.00, 99.00, 86.87, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25 06:18:11', '2026-08-25 06:18:11', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(119, NULL, 108, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To increase the firefighting water storage tank capacity to at least 30 m³ to ensure an adequate water supply for firefighting purposes.\r\nb. To maintain the fire alarm system, including the control panel, in good working condition at all times.\r\nc.  To increase the CCTV system storage capacity to retain surveillance footage for a minimum period of 90 days.\r\nd. To provide and maintain a sufficient quantity of dry firefighting sand together with at least two shovels.\r\ne. To install clearly visible entrance and exit signs made of illuminated retro-reflective materials and ensure they are readable from a minimum distance of 50 meters.\r\nf. To employ trained security personnel from a registered security company.\r\ng. To conduct periodic testing of the lightning protection system at least once every six (6) months and maintain valid test records for inspection.\r\nh. To immediately stop all cooking activities within the petrol station premises, as such activities are not authorized.\r\ni. To send copies of the following valid documents to the City of Kigali via info@kigalicity.gov.rw: valid Electrical Installation Compliance Certificate; Retail License; and Valid Insurance within two weeks.', NULL, NULL, 69.50, 100.00, 69.50, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25 14:00:37', '2026-08-26 05:27:50', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(120, NULL, 109, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To provide  additional one (1) 9 kg Foam Fire Extinguisher and one (1) 25 kg Dry Chemical Powder (DCP) Fire Extinguisher.\r\nb. To complete the installation of the water-based firefighting system, including a water storage tank, hose reel, and a dedicated firefighting water pump capable of maintaining a minimum pressure of 8 bar.\r\nc. To display emergency hotline numbers (Police, Fire Brigade, and Ambulance).\r\nd. To install clearly visible entrance and exit signs made of illuminated retro-reflective materials and ensure that they are readable from a minimum distance of 50 meters.\r\ne. To install  appropriate warning signs that are clearly visible from a minimum distance of 7.5 meters.\r\nf. To install an emergency stop switch at an easily accessible location for use during emergencies.\r\ng. To conduct periodic testing of the lightning protection system at least once every six (6) months and maintain valid test records for inspection.\r\nh. To send copies of the following valid documents to the City of Kigali via info@kigalicity.gov.rw within two weeks: electrical installation compliance certificate; construction permit; occupation permit; fuel tank calibration certificate; dispenser test certificate; and valid insurance certificate.', NULL, NULL, 48.50, 100.00, 48.50, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25 14:20:33', '2026-08-26 05:47:22', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(121, NULL, 110, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To provide additional one (1) 9 kg Foam Fire Extinguisher.\r\nb. To install a firefighting water pump capable of maintaining a pressure between 8 and 15 bar to ensure adequate water pressure for firefighting purposes.\r\nc. To provide  dry fine sand with at least two shovels.\r\nd. To increase the CCTV system storage capacity to retain surveillance footage for a minimum period of 90 days.\r\ne. To install clearly visible entrance and exit signs made of illuminated retro-reflective materials and ensure they are readable from a minimum distance of 50 meters.\r\nf. To conduct periodic testing of the lightning protection system at least once every six (6) months and maintain valid test records for inspection.\r\ng. To provide at least two changing rooms, one for male staff and one for female staff.\r\nh. To send copies of the following valid documents to the City of Kigali via info@kigalicity.gov.rw within two weeks: electrical installation compliance certificate; occupation permit; fuel tank calibration certificate; dispenser test certificate; retail license; and valid insurance.', NULL, NULL, 62.50, 100.00, 62.50, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-25 14:41:00', '2026-08-26 06:00:07', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(122, NULL, 111, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-27', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To maintain  hose reel system in good working condition and ensure that it remains fully operational.\r\nb. To increase  water storage tank capacity to a minimum of 30 m³.\r\nc. To maintain the fire alarm system and rectify any faults or defects identified in the system.\r\nd. To display emergency contact numbers (Police, Fire Brigade, and Ambulance).\r\ne. To hire trained security staff from a registered security company.\r\nf. To make CCTV control room accessible and ensure that surveillance footage is retained for a minimum period of 90 days.\r\ng. To send copies of the following valid documents to the City of Kigali via info@kigalicity.gov.rw within two weeks: occupation permit; construction permit; environmental impact assessment (EIA) certificate; electrical installation compliance certificate; fuel tank calibration certificate; dispenser test certificate; retail license; and valid insurance.\r\nh. To conduct periodic testing of the lightning protection system at least once every six (6) months and keep valid test records for inspection.', NULL, NULL, 63.00, 100.00, 63.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-27 11:33:55', '2026-08-27 12:47:39', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(123, NULL, 112, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-27', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To maintain fire alarm system, including the control panel, in good working condition at all times.\r\nb. To send copies of the following valid documents to the City of Kigali via info@kigalicity.gov.rw within two weeks: electrical installation compliance certificate; construction permit; occupation permit; fuel tank calibration certificate; dispenser test certificate; retail license; environmental impact assessment (EIA) certificate; and valid insurance.\r\nc. To provide  additional one (1) 9 kg foam fire extinguisher, and refill or replace all expired fire extinguishers.\r\nd. To provide  dry fine sand  with at least two shovels.\r\ne. To maintain the water-based firefighting system, including the firefighting water pump.\r\nf. To increase  water storage tank capacity to at least 30 m³.\r\ng. To establish a CCTV control room and increase the CCTV storage capacity to retain surveillance footage for a minimum period of 90 days.\r\nh. To install clearly visible warning signs and pictograms, and display an emergency evacuation plan.\r\ni. To conduct periodic testing of the lightning protection system at least once every six (6) months and maintain valid test records for inspection.', NULL, NULL, 50.00, 100.00, 50.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-27 12:16:36', '2026-08-27 13:00:54', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
