(143, NULL, 138, NULL, 'waste_water', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 23, 'MUNYANEZA Honeste', 3, '1. No ventilation pipe\r\n2. No evidence of wastewater discharge from septic tank, but based on WASAC receipts of water 67 m3 per month, current water consumption was estimated 2 m3 per day which does not reasonate with size and emptying of the septic tank.', '1. Installing the ventilation pipe on the septic tank\r\n2. Disconnecting moping water from the discharged rain water, current measures of using buckets in mopping are not adequate', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01 11:07:32', '2026-09-01 11:07:32', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(144, NULL, 139, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 7, 'SENZIRA Eugene', 2, 'The petrol station does not comply with fire safety and security system', 'To Install a water tank with 30m³ capacity and increase fire pump to a minimum of 8 bar.\r\nTo Install a fire hydrant with 41mm hose.Provide additional fire extinguishers: 25kg DCP, 9kg CO₂, and 9kg Foam. \r\nTo Refill all expired fire extinguishers.Provide a sand bucket in the store.\r\nTo Upgrade CCTV camera storage to 3 months.\r\nTo Provide an emergency evacuation plan, assembly points, and exit signs.\r\nTo Remove kitchen and all food preparation activities from the station.\r\nTo Test the lightning protection system every 6 months by a licensed engineer.\r\nTo Install illuminated entrance and exit signs.\r\nTo Avail the following mandatory documents: Occupation Permit, Retail License, and Valid Insurance. Send to info@kigalicity.gov.rw.\r\nTo Find a waste collection area which is sheltered.\r\nTo Repair the plumbing system in the washroom.\r\nTo Provide separate changing rooms for males and females and label them.\r\nTo Remove the bed inside the female bathroom.\r\nTo immediately cease hot water discharge in the public drainage.\r\nTo Install signs for public toilets.\r\nN.B: All recommendations should be implemented in no more than 15 days from today.', NULL, NULL, 52.50, 100.00, 52.50, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01 11:34:14', '2026-09-02 05:44:24', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(145, NULL, 140, NULL, 'waste_water', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 24, 'UWERA Marie Josee', 2, '- No contract with emptying company (tank is about to be full)\r\n- Wastewater generated from the shaving salon is discharged into the soil through a soak pit.\r\n- Inaccessible septic tanks manholes due to construction materials stored in their room', '- Install STP \r\n- Engage a licensed emptying company for regular emptying of septic tank \r\n- Provide work plan of STP Installation within three days to the CoK \r\n- Ensure that the septic tank manholes are accessible (relocate these construction materials ie tiles)', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01 12:01:19', '2026-09-01 12:01:24', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(146, NULL, 141, NULL, 'waste_water', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 24, 'UWERA Marie Josee', 2, '1. Discharge of untreated wastewater ( wastewater from toilet)into wetland \r\n2.sewage treatment plant which doesn\'t have complete chambers \r\n3.Cleaning  Wastewater from super factory are discharged directly into environment', '1. To stop immediately discharging untreated wastewater and work with wastewater emptying company by keeping record \r\n2.To close all pipes that release untreated wastewater in wetland area(outlet pipe)\r\n3 . Upgrading current sewage treatment plant \r\n4. To catch all cleaning wastewater from super factory \r\n5. To provide work plan of upgrading STP to city of Kigali within 3 days (3/9/2026', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 0.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01 12:31:04', '2026-09-01 12:31:08', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(147, NULL, 142, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-31', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To provide one additional 9 kg Dry Chemical Powder (DCP) fire extinguisher and one 25 kg DCP  fire extinguisher, and ensure that all expired fire extinguishers are refilled and maintained.\r\nb. To provide dry fine sand with at least two shovels.\r\nc. To install a fully functional fire alarm system with a control panel.\r\nd. To install  CCTV camera with an accessible control room at the petrol station and ensure that recorded footage is retained for a minimum period of 90 days.\r\ne. To install a firefighting water pump capable of delivering 8-15 bar pressure and increase the fire water storage tank capacity to at least 30 m³.\r\nf. To submit the following valid documents to the City of Kigali through info@kigalicity.gov.rw within two weeks: electrical installation compliance certificate, occupation permit, fuel tank calibration certificate, fuel dispenser test certificate, retail license, and valid insurance.\r\ng. To conduct periodic testing of Para lightning system and ensure that all test records and maintenance logs are properly documented and available for inspection.\r\nh. To make the sanitary facilities accessible to all users, including persons with disabilities, and provide at least two changing rooms in compliance with applicable safety and accessibility requirements.', NULL, NULL, 55.00, 100.00, 55.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01 12:41:13', '2026-09-10 13:51:52', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(148, NULL, 143, 2, 'petrol', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01', 'new', NULL, 1, 'completed', 9, 'UWIKUNDA Idesbald', 3, NULL, 'a. To provide additional one (1) 9 kg Foam Fire Extinguisher, one (1) 9 kg CO₂ Fire Extinguisher, and one (1) 25 kg DCP (Dry Chemical Powder) Fire Extinguisher to ensure adequate fire protection coverage.\r\nb. To avail dry fire sand together with two shovels for emergency firefighting purposes.\r\nc. To increase the CCTV camera storage capacity to a minimum of 90 days.\r\nd. To increase the water storage tank capacity to at least 30 m³ to ensure an adequate water supply for firefighting operations.\r\ne. To conduct periodic testing and maintenance of the lightning protection system and make the latest test and maintenance records available for inspection.\r\nf. To submit the following valid documents to the City of Kigali via info@kigalicity.gov.rw within two (2) weeks: electrical installation compliance certificate; occupation permit; fuel tank calibration certificate; fuel tank calibration certificate; fuel dispenser test certificate, valid retail license; and valid insurance.', NULL, NULL, 69.50, 100.00, 69.50, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-01 13:26:17', '2026-09-10 14:06:16', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
